      "writtenOn": "2024-08-06T01:55:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As discussed the system_server can\u0027t support working with different Tethering services that restart, as state will be out-of-sync and this is not a tested/supported use-case. When Tethering crashes (a system bug) the system_server is expected to crash to recover to a working state, otherwise the device may get unstable behavior for a long time instead of recovering immediately.\n\nIf you add the \"alive\" checks in the 2 places suggested above this should allow ensuring that after system_server restart, it can properly fetch an alive connector.",
      "revId": "a2bf70e8631cbc127aba6259d07d9e9d6ad29f53",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
